  "title": "General Aamaal of each Month",
  "code": "012",
  "tabs": [
    "Dua 43 of Saheefah Kaamelah\nThe general rites to be advisably done in each month are as follows:\nFirst: It is recommended to say the famous supplicatory prayers at the sight of the new moon. The most preferable of these is the [supplication No. 43 of al-Saheefah al-Sajjaadiyyah](AA21), which has been mentioned within the rites at the beginning of month of Ramazan.",
    "Surah Faatehah 7 times\nSecond: It is recommended to recite Surah al-Faatehah seven times in order to escape eye ache.",
    "Eating Cheese\nThird: It is recommended to have some cheese, for it has been narrated that one who usually eats some cheese at the beginning of each month will have almost all his requests answered.",
    "Namaz of 1st Night\nFourth: At the first night of each month, it is recommended to offer a two unit prayer with [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) and [Surah al-An’am (No. 6)](A10). One may then pray Almighty Allah to save him from any terror or pain and to make him live throughout that month peacefully and safely.",
    "Namaz of 1st Day\nFifth: On the first day of each month, it is recommended to offer a two unit prayer in the first unit of which, [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) is recited once and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) repeated thirty times. In the second unit, [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) is recited once and [Surah al-Qadr](A101) repeated thirty times. After accomplishment, alms should be given. Whoever offers this prayer each month, will win safety throughout that month. According to other narrations, the following supplicatory prayer, which is a number of Quranic verses, may be said after the accomplishment of the prayer:\nبِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nوَمَا مِنْ دَآ بَّةٍ فِى الْاَرْضِ اِلَّا عَلَى اللّٰهِ رِزْقُهَا وَ يَعْلَمُ مُسْتَقَرَّهَا وَمُسْتَوْدَعَهَاؕ كُلٌّ فِىْ كِتٰبٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(6)\nWA MAA MIN DAAA-BBATIN FIL ARZI ILLAA A’LAL LAAHE RIZQOHAA WA YA’LAMO MUSTAQARRAHAA WA MUSTAWDA-A’HAA KULLUN FEE KETAABIM MOBEEN.\nThere is no moving creature on earth but its sustenance dependeth on Allah: He knoweth the time and place of its definite abode and its temporary deposit: All is in a clear Record.\nبِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nوَاِنْ يَّمْسَسْكَ اللّٰهُ بِضُرٍّ فَلَا كَاشِفَ لَهٗۤ اِلَّا هُوَ ۚ وَاِنْ يُّرِدْكَ بِخَيْرٍ فَلَا رَآدَّ لِفَضْلِهٖ ؕ يُصِيْبُ بِهٖ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ مِنْ عِبَادِهٖ ؕ وَهُوَ الْغَفُوْرُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(107)\nIf Allah do touch thee with hurt, there is none can remove it but He: if He do design some benefit for thee, there is none can keep back His favour: He causeth it to reach whomsoever of His servants He pleaseth. And He is the Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful.\nبِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nسَيَجْعَلُ اللّٰهُ بَعْدَ عُسْرٍ يُسْرًا \nSAYAJ-A’LUL LAAHO BA_A’DA U’SRIN YUSRAN \nAllah will bring about, after hardship, ease.\nمَا شَاۤءَ اللّٰهُ لَا قُوَّةَ اِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ \nMAA SHAAA-AL LAAHO LAA QUWWATA ILLAA BILAAHE\nWhat Allah wills [will come to pass]; there is no power except through Allah.\nحَسْبُنَا اللّٰهُ وَ نِعْمَ الْوَكِيْلُ \nHASBONAL LAAHO WA NE’MAL WAKEELO\nSufficient for us is Allah, and He is the best Disposer of affairs.\nوَ اُفَوِّضُ اَمْرِيْۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ بَصِيْرٌ ۢ بِالْعِبَادِ \nWA OFAWWEZO AMREEE ILAL LAAHE INNAL LAAHA BASEERUM BIL-E’BAADE\nAnd I entrust my affair to Allah. Indeed, Allah is All-Seeing of His servants.\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْتَ سُبْحَانَكَ اِنِّيْۤ كُنْتُ مِنَ الظَّالِمِيْنَ \nLAAA ELAAHA ILLAAA ANTA SUBHAANAKA INNEE KUNTO MENAZ ZAALEMEENA \nThere is no god except You; Exalted are You. Indeed, I have been of the wrongdoers.\nرَبِّ اِنِّيْ لِمَاۤ اَنْزَلْتَ اِلَيَّ مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَقِيْرٌ \nRABBE INNEE LEMAAA ANZALTA ELAYYA MIN KHAYRIN FAQEERUN \nMy Lord, indeed I am, for whatever good You would send down to me, in desperate need.\nرَبِّ لَا تَذَرْنِيْ فَرْدًا وَّ اَنْتَ خَيْرُ الْوَارِثِيْنَ.\nRABBE LAA TAZARNEE FARDANW WA ANTA KHAYRUL WAARESEENA.\nMy Lord, do not leave me alone [without an heir], while You are the best of inheritors."
